          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy with focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. Seizure onset was at 18 years of age. The epilepsy has a genetic etiology, with a causative PCDH19 variant, c.918G>A. The epilepsy is drug responsive.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Zonisamide\n- Levetiracetam\n\nSeizure Burden:\nApproximately 2 seizures per year.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-responsive focal epilepsy with focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures, associated with the causative PCDH19 c.918G>A variant.\n\nPlan:\nContinue zonisamide and levetiracetam. Continue monitoring seizure frequency and follow up in the epilepsy clinic.",
